        "818": {"comment":"Done"},
        "819": {"synopsis":"Sets up the devices of unit D and gives their units bank E (NextZXOS ROM 2's IDE_MOUNT,\nthrough IDE_MOUNT_UNITS):\n1. (HL) = E, then CALL_TABLE's first entry (DEVICES_INIT) for unit D; port $E3 = 0 after it.\n2. (HL) = $FF; then E is written to as many bytes from HL on as DEVICES_INIT left in B, D\n   counting up from the unit.\nExit: carry set, HL past the bytes written; carry clear when D reaches 16. DE kept.","comment":"Unit, bank kept"},
        "821": {"comment":"The bank at HL"},
        "822": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "823": {"comment":"DEVICES_INIT for it"},
        "826": {"comment":"Port $E3 = 0"},
        "829": {"comment":"HL, DE back"},
        "831": {"comment":"$FF at HL"},
        "833": {"comment":"B + 1: B bytes"},
        "834": {"comment":"Into the count"},
        "836": {"synopsis":"One unit's byte.","comment":"Unit 16 or more?"},
        "839": {"comment":"Yes: carry clear"},
        "840": {"comment":"Its byte = the bank"},
        "842": {"comment":"Next unit"},
        "843": {"comment":"Until B bytes written","synopsis":"UNITS_INIT's count: one more unit while B lasts."},
        "845": {"comment":"Success"},
        "847": {"synopsis":"Reads the drive part of a name at HL: an optional user area (one or two digits, 0-15), an\noptional drive letter A-P (either case) and a ':'. Without the ':' none of it is taken.\nNextZXOS ROM 2 calls it for every name it passes.\n1. Digits: E = their value, with bit 7 set when it is below 16; two digits making 16 or more\n   are not taken (HL back to the start).\n2. A letter: D = 0-15, bit 6 of E set.\n3. The next character must be ':' (HL then past it); otherwise E = 0 and HL is left where it\n   was.\n4. No letter: D = the default drive ($2007).\n5. No user area: DRIVE_USER_AREA for the drive (D = $FF), or 0 when that fails.\nExit: A = the user area in bits 7-4, the drive in bits 3-0; HL past the ':' or as on entry.\nDE kept.","comment":"DE kept"},
        "848": {"comment":"Start kept"},
        "849": {"comment":"No number yet"},
        "851": {"comment":"A digit?"},
        "854": {"comment":"No: on to the letter"},
        "856": {"comment":"A second one?"},
        "859": {"comment":"The number"},
        "860": {"comment":"16 or more?"},
        "862": {"comment":"Yes: not taken"},
        "864": {"comment":"No: bit 7, a user area"},
        "866": {"comment":"On"},
        "868": {"comment":"HL back to the start","synopsis":"A number of 16 or more: HL back to the name's start, no number taken."},
        "870": {"synopsis":"The drive letter, if there is one.","comment":"Capital"},
        "871": {"comment":"A-P?"},
        "875": {"comment":"Below 'A'"},
        "877": {"comment":"Past 'P'?"},
        "879": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "881": {"comment":"D = 0-15"},
        "882": {"comment":"Past it"},
        "883": {"comment":"Bit 6: a letter"},
        "885": {"comment":"Next character","synopsis":"NAME_PREP's step 3: a ':' must follow, else nothing is taken."},
        "887": {"comment":"A ':'?"},
        "889": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "891": {"comment":"No: nothing taken"},
        "893": {"comment":"On"},
        "895": {"comment":"Past the ':' as the HL to return","synopsis":"The ':' found: HL past it becomes the HL returned."},
        "896": {"comment":"A letter given?","synopsis":"NAME_PREP's step 4: the default drive when no letter was given."},
        "898": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "900": {"comment":"No: the default drive"},
        "904": {"comment":"A = the user area","synopsis":"NAME_PREP's step 5: the user area given, or DRIVE_USER_AREA's."},
        "907": {"comment":"One given?"},
        "909": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "911": {"comment":"DE kept"},
