        "1410": {"comment":"DEBC = the cluster"},
        "1417": {"comment":"Place kept"},
        "1418": {"comment":"DEBC = the next cluster"},
        "1421": {"comment":"Place back"},
        "1422": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "1423": {"comment":"A cluster of the volume?"},
        "1426": {"comment":"rc_eof"},
        "1428": {"comment":"No: the chain has ended"},
        "1429": {"comment":"Stored back"},
        "1437": {"comment":"Count = 0"},
        "1439": {"comment":"Success"},
        "1441": {"synopsis":"Is DEBC a cluster number of volume IX: 2 or more and no more than its highest cluster\n(IX+$22-$25)? HL kept.\nExit: carry set if so; carry clear if not (Z for 0 and 1).","comment":"Low byte"},
        "1442": {"comment":"Below 2?"},
        "1444": {"comment":"No: check the top"},
        "1446": {"comment":"The rest 0 too?"},
        "1449": {"comment":"Yes: 0 or 1, carry clear"},
        "1450": {"synopsis":"Carry set when DEBC is no more than the highest cluster (IX+$22-$25). From $0C60 too.","comment":"HL kept"},
        "1451": {"comment":"Highest cluster, low word"},
        "1457": {"comment":"Less DEBC's"},
        "1460": {"comment":"High word"},
        "1466": {"comment":"Less DEBC's, with the borrow"},
        "1468": {"comment":"Carry: DEBC not above it"},
        "1469": {"comment":"HL back"},
        "1471": {"synopsis":"Takes a free cluster on volume IX:\n1. From the one after the last taken (IX+$2F) on, cluster by cluster, wrapping from the\n   highest back to 2, until one whose FAT entry is 0 (its top 4 bits ignored); coming round\n   to the start fails with rc_diskfull ($1A).\n2. It becomes the last taken; the free count (IX+$2B-$2E) goes down by one.\n3. Its FAT entry = $0FFFFFFF, the chain's end (FAT_WRITE), then $0EAC.\nCalled from CHAIN_EXTEND and $1497.\nExit: carry set, DEBC = the cluster; carry clear, A = the code.","comment":"DEBC = the last taken"},
        "1475": {"synopsis":"The next cluster.","comment":"Plus one, 32 bits"},
        "1485": {"comment":"A cluster of the volume?","synopsis":"CLUSTER_ALLOC: past the highest cluster, back to cluster 2."},
        "1488": {"comment":"Yes"},
        "1490": {"comment":"No: back to cluster 2"},
        "1496": {"comment":"Back at the start?","synopsis":"CLUSTER_ALLOC: coming back to the start fails with rc_diskfull."},
        "1518": {"comment":"rc_diskfull"},
        "1520": {"comment":"Yes: none free"},
        "1521": {"comment":"Cluster kept","synopsis":"CLUSTER_ALLOC: the candidate's FAT entry read."},
        "1523": {"comment":"DEBC = its FAT entry"},
        "1526": {"comment":"Read"},
        "1528": {"comment":"Failed: drop, return"},
        "1531": {"comment":"Entry 0: free?","synopsis":"CLUSTER_ALLOC: an entry of 0 is free, otherwise the next cluster."},
        "1537": {"comment":"Cluster back"},
        "1539": {"comment":"No: next"},
        "1541": {"comment":"The last taken"},
        "1545": {"comment":"Free count less one"},
        "1558": {"comment":"Low word went to $FFFF?"},
        "1561": {"comment":"No"},
        "1563": {"comment":"Yes: the high word too"},
        "1576": {"comment":"Cluster kept","synopsis":"CLUSTER_ALLOC's step 3: the new cluster's FAT entry = $0FFFFFFF, then $0EAC."},
        "1578": {"comment":"IY kept"},
        "1580": {"comment":"$0FFFFFFF: the chain's end"},
        "1587": {"comment":"Into its FAT entry"},
