        "1795": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from HL to DE as LDIR does, but when DE is below $4000 each write is made\nwith port $E3 = A (DivMMC RAM), port $E3 as it was for the reads: first BC's low 2 bits one\nat a time, then four at a time. A destination of $4000 or above is a plain LDIR. Called from\n$1E86 (and by NextZXOS ROM 2 with A = 9).\nExit: HL and DE past the bytes, BC = 0. The alternate registers kept.","comment":"Port value kept"},
