        "1897": {"synopsis":"Copies BC bytes from HL to DE as LDIR does, but when HL is below $4000 each byte is read\nwith port $E3 = A (DivMMC RAM), port $E3 as it was for the writes. A source of $4000 or\nabove is a plain LDIR. Called from $1E05.\nExit: HL and DE past the bytes, BC = 0. The alternate registers kept.","comment":"Port value kept"},
