        "3254": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "3256": {"comment":"256 entries"},
        "3258": {"comment":"FAT16?"},
        "3264": {"comment":"FAT32: 128 entries"},
        "3266": {"synopsis":"One FAT32 entry.","comment":"Four bytes ORed"},
        "3275": {"comment":"The top 4 bits ignored"},
        "3278": {"comment":"Free: one more"},
        "3281": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "3285": {"synopsis":"One FAT16 entry.","comment":"FAT16: two bytes ORed"},
        "3289": {"comment":"Free: one more"},
        "3292": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "3294": {"synopsis":"The next FAT sector, BC:DE + 1.","comment":"The count, the sector back"},
        "3297": {"comment":"Next sector"},
        "3303": {"synopsis":"IY:HL, the sectors left, less one.","comment":"One sector fewer to go"},
        "3311": {"synopsis":"IY:HL 0: all read.","comment":"Any left?"},
        "3319": {"synopsis":"BCDE = the free cluster count of the volume at IX (IX+$2B; $FFFF0000 when not known, as\n$09CC tests), carry set.","comment":"BCDE = the free count"},
        "3323": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3325": {"synopsis":"Read error: the stacked words dropped, carry clear.","comment":"Clean the stack"},
        "3329": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITON_READ (the vector at $010C; so spelt in the API document): builds a 64-byte\npartition entry for partition BC of unit A at HL, the partition mounted on the scratch\ndescriptor at $203E by $0A5D.\n1. Byte 0: '0' + its slot in the partition table (0 with none), byte 1 '>'.\n2. Bytes 2-12: the volume label returned by $0A5D, then three spaces.\n3. Byte 16: the type, $10 for FAT16, $11 for FAT32; then six $FF bytes.\n4. Bytes 23-26: the size from IX+7; the 37 bytes to the end 0.\nEntry: A = the unit, BC = the partition (0 the first), HL = the buffer.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error. BC and IX kept.","comment":"Kept"},
        "3333": {"comment":"The scratch descriptor"},
        "3337": {"comment":"Mount the partition"},
        "3341": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "3343": {"comment":"Its slot in the table"},
        "3346": {"comment":"As a digit"},
        "3350": {"comment":"Then '>'"},
        "3353": {"comment":"The label's 11 bytes"},
        "3360": {"comment":"Three spaces"},
        "3362": {"synopsis":"One space."},
        "3367": {"comment":"The type: $10"},
        "3369": {"comment":"FAT16?"},
        "3375": {"comment":"FAT32: $11"},
        "3376": {"synopsis":"Six $FF bytes after the type."},
        "3377": {"comment":"Six $FF bytes"},
        "3379": {"synopsis":"One $FF."},
        "3384": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "3385": {"comment":"HL = IX+7, the size"},
        "3392": {"comment":"Four bytes"},
        "3396": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "3397": {"comment":"37 zeros (C is 0)"},
        "3399": {"synopsis":"One 0."},
        "3403": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3404": {"synopsis":"BC and IX restored.","comment":"Restored"},
        "3408": {"synopsis":"IDE_PARTITION_FIND (the vector at $0109): finds the partition of unit A named at HL by\nbuilding each partition's entry at $2200 (PART_ENTRY_READ) in turn.\n1. A name with '>' as its second byte is matched on all 16 bytes ('p>' and the label);\nwhen only its label part is blank, 'p>' alone decides.\n2. Otherwise the 14 bytes of the label part are matched; an all-blank name matches the\nfirst partition.\nEntry: A = the unit, HL = the name.\nExit: carry set and BC = the partition number (its volume mounted on $203E); or carry\nclear and A = the error of the first partition not there ($38).","comment":"The first partition"},
        "3411": {"synopsis":"One partition's entry built and compared.","comment":"Unit, number, name stacked"},
        "3414": {"comment":"Its entry built here"},
        "3420": {"comment":"The name"},
        "3421": {"comment":"No more partitions"},
        "3424": {"comment":"The name's second byte"},
        "3426": {"comment":"'>'?"},
        "3430": {"comment":"Compare 16 bytes"},
        "3433": {"comment":"From the entry's start"},
        "3436": {"comment":"Carry: the full form"},
        "3439": {"comment":"Otherwise 14 bytes"},
        "3441": {"comment":"From the label"},
        "3443": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "3444": {"synopsis":"One byte compared.","comment":"A byte of the entry"},
        "3446": {"comment":"Same as the name's?"},
        "3450": {"comment":"More to compare?"},
        "3453": {"synopsis":"A match: BC = the partition number, carry set.","comment":"Found: BC = the number"},
        "3456": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3458": {"synopsis":"A difference: in the full form at the label's first byte, a blank label still matches.","comment":"Label form: no match"},
        "3460": {"comment":"The label's first byte?"},
        "3465": {"comment":"Is the name's label all spaces?"},
        "3470": {"synopsis":"One byte of the label: a space?"},
        "3476": {"comment":"Yes: a match"},
        "3478": {"synopsis":"The next partition.","comment":"Next partition"},
        "3484": {"synopsis":"No partition left: carry clear, A = the mount error.","comment":"Drop number and unit"},
        "3487": {"synopsis":"The partition is mounted already: A = $3B (rc_partopen), three words dropped."},
        "3488": {"synopsis":"Two words dropped; IX restored, carry as it is."},
        "3493": {"synopsis":"Maps drive E to partition BC of unit D (the vector at $010F, reached from the jump at\n$0169 by IDE_DOS_MAP's call in ROM 2).\n1. Every mapped drive (the 16-word table at $2E6E, DIR_REC pointers) is checked: one on the\nsame partition (IX+$11) of the same unit (bit 0 of IX+$10) gives error $3B.\n2. The drive's descriptor ($2A10 + 53 x E) is mounted by $0A5D.\n3. Its directory record ($2D60 + 15 x E) is set to the root (DIR_REC_ROOT) and its address\nstored in the drive's word of $2E6E.\nEntry: E = the drive 0-15, D = the unit, BC = the partition.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error. IX kept.","comment":"Kept"},
        "3495": {"comment":"A = the drive, E = drive + 1"},
        "3498": {"comment":"HL = its word in the drive table"},
        "3502": {"comment":"Stacked, then unit and drive"},
        "3504": {"comment":"Drive 0"},
        "3505": {"synopsis":"One drive of the table checked.","comment":"Drive number stacked"},
        "3506": {"comment":"Is it mapped?"},
        "3511": {"comment":"HL = its directory record"},
        "3512": {"comment":"DE = the record's descriptor"},
        "3515": {"comment":"IY = it"},
        "3518": {"comment":"Same partition?"},
        "3530": {"comment":"Unit and drive"},
        "3534": {"comment":"Its unit"},
        "3539": {"comment":"Same unit?"},
        "3540": {"comment":"rc_partopen"},
        "3544": {"synopsis":"The next drive, up to 15.","comment":"Next drive"},
        "3546": {"comment":"16 drives"},
        "3550": {"comment":"D = the unit, E = drive + 1"},
        "3552": {"comment":"Descriptors: $2A10 + 53 x drive"},
        "3559": {"synopsis":"53 bytes per drive."},
        "3564": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "3565": {"comment":"Mount partition BC"},
        "3568": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "3570": {"comment":"E = drive + 1"},
        "3571": {"comment":"Records: $2D60 + 15 x drive"},
        "3578": {"synopsis":"15 bytes per drive."},
        "3583": {"comment":"The record at the root"},
        "3586": {"comment":"The drive's word"},
        "3587": {"comment":"= the record"},
        "3594": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3595": {"synopsis":"IX restored.","comment":"Restored"},
        "3598": {"synopsis":"Unmaps drive A (the vector at $0121, reached from the jump at $016C by IDE_DOS_UNMAP in\nROM 2): error $24 (rc_inuse) while one of the 17 six-byte entries at $2EB4 with bit 7 of\nits first byte set names the drive in its last byte, or an open file handle (16 of 45\nbytes at $2740, byte $0F not 0) is on the drive's descriptor. Otherwise the drive's word\nin the table at $2E6E is cleared.\nEntry: A = the drive 0-15.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = $24.","comment":"The table at $2EB4"},
        "3601": {"comment":"17 entries"},
        "3603": {"synopsis":"One entry of the table at $2EB4.","comment":"In use?"},
        "3608": {"comment":"Its last byte"},
        "3612": {"comment":"This drive?"},
        "3616": {"synopsis":"The next entry, 6 bytes on.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "3622": {"comment":"HL = the drive's word"},
        "3626": {"comment":"DE = its record's descriptor"},
        "3630": {"comment":"The file handles"},
        "3634": {"comment":"16"},
        "3636": {"synopsis":"One file handle.","comment":"Open?"},
        "3642": {"comment":"Its descriptor"},
        "3648": {"comment":"On this drive?"},
        "3652": {"synopsis":"In use: A = $24, carry clear.","comment":"Drop the word"},
        "3653": {"comment":"rc_inuse"},
        "3656": {"synopsis":"The next handle, 45 bytes on.","comment":"Next handle"},
        "3665": {"comment":"The drive's word"},
        "3666": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "3670": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3672": {"synopsis":"The text of drive A's mapping at BC (the vector at $011E, used by IDE_DOS_MAPPING in ROM\n2): the unit digit, '>', then the first 16 bytes of the partition's entry (PART_ENTRY_READ:\nthe slot digit, '>', the label and three spaces), and $FF. The drive's word at $2E6E is\nnot tested here.\nEntry: A = the drive 0-15, BC = the buffer.\nExit: carry set, A = the unit (bit 1 of IX+$10 cleared), BC = the partition, DE = the\n$FF's address; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"DE = the drive's record"},
        "3676": {"comment":"DE = its descriptor"},
        "3679": {"comment":"IY = it"},
        "3682": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "3685": {"comment":"Without the block-address bit"},
        "3688": {"comment":"As a digit"},
        "3692": {"comment":"Then '>'"},
        "3696": {"comment":"The unit"},
        "3697": {"comment":"The buffer stacked"},
        "3698": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "3701": {"comment":"BC = the partition number"},
        "3703": {"comment":"Its entry at $2200"},
        "3711": {"comment":"DE = the buffer"},
        "3712": {"comment":"Failed"},
        "3713": {"comment":"The partition kept"},
        "3714": {"comment":"16 bytes of the entry"},
        "3719": {"comment":"Then $FF"},
        "3723": {"comment":"A = the unit"},
        "3727": {"synopsis":"DOS_FLUSH (the vector at $011B): each open file handle (byte $0F not 0) is brought up to\ndate by $16BF, then the sector cache written out ($08D1). The drive passed in A is not\nlooked at: every handle is done.\nExit: as $08D1. IX and IY kept.","comment":"Kept"},
        "3731": {"comment":"16 handles"},
        "3733": {"synopsis":"One handle."},
        "3734": {"comment":"Handle B - 1"},
        "3736": {"comment":"Selected"},
        "3739": {"comment":"Open?"},
        "3743": {"comment":"Write its state out"},
        "3746": {"comment":"Next"},
        "3753": {"comment":"The cache out"},
        "3756": {"synopsis":"On a FAT32 volume with an FSInfo sector (bit 6 of IX+$13), copies the free count and the\nnext-free hint (IX+$2B, 8 bytes) to its bytes $1E8-$1EF in the cache and marks the sector\nfor writing ($08E2).\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error. BC, DE, HL kept.","comment":"FSInfo in use?"},
        "3760": {"comment":"No: nothing to do"},
        "3765": {"comment":"DE = its sector"},
        "3769": {"comment":"High word 0"},
        "3772": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "3775": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "3777": {"comment":"Its free count at $1E8"},
        "3782": {"comment":"From IX+$2B"},
        "3789": {"comment":"8 bytes"},
        "3794": {"comment":"Mark the sector changed"},
        "3797": {"comment":"Success"},
        "3798": {"synopsis":"BC, DE and HL restored."},
        "3802": {"synopsis":"IDE_DRIVE (the vector at $0103): IX = 0, no handle for a unit.","comment":"No unit handle"},
        "3807": {"synopsis":"IDE_CAPACITY (the vector at $0106): IX = $00FC, then ROM2_SD_SIZE.","comment":"Passed to SD_CAPACITY"},
        "3811": {"synopsis":"Runs ROM 2's $17DE (SD_CAPACITY: the size of SD card C from its CSD register) through\n$03F8: NextReg $8E = 2 and the RET at $1FF9 leave the DivMMC memory; $3CFC there brings\nit back. Also from $0A43, which ORs the B it returns (2 for a block-addressed card) into\nIX+$10.\nEntry: C = the card, 0 or 1.\nExit: as SD_CAPACITY: carry set and DE:HL = the size in 512-byte sectors; or carry clear.","comment":"ROM 2's SD_CAPACITY"},
        "3814": {"comment":"Run it in ROM 2"},
        "3817": {"synopsis":"The label 'NO NAME' padded to 11 bytes with spaces: $0A5D's answer for a volume whose boot\nsector has no extended signature."},
        "3828": {"synopsis":"The checksum of the 11-byte short name at HL that ties long-name entries to it: each byte\nadded to the sum rotated right.\nExit: A = the checksum. HL kept; B = 0."},
        "3829": {"comment":"Sum 0"},
        "3830": {"comment":"11 bytes"},
        "3832": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"Rotated right, plus the byte"},
        "3835": {"comment":"Next"},
        "3839": {"synopsis":"Takes the 13 characters of the long-name entry at HL, last first, into the text that ends\nat DE (bytes $1C-$1F, $0E-$19, $01-$0A of the entry, two bytes each): a character 0 or\n$FFFF is left out; one not in $20-$7E becomes '_'.\nExit: DE = the text's new start.","comment":"The entry's last byte"},
        "3843": {"comment":"Characters 12-13"},
        "3848": {"comment":"Skip bytes $1A-$1B"},
        "3850": {"comment":"Characters 6-11"},
        "3855": {"comment":"Skip bytes $0B-$0D"},
        "3858": {"comment":"Characters 1-5"},
        "3860": {"synopsis":"One 16-bit character, high byte first.","comment":"A = the high byte"},
        "3862": {"comment":"C = the low byte"},
        "3864": {"comment":"High byte 0?"},
        "3867": {"comment":"$FFFF: padding"},
        "3869": {"comment":"Leave it out"},
        "3871": {"comment":"Otherwise '_'"},
        "3873": {"synopsis":"High byte 0: the low byte as it is unless 0.","comment":"The low byte"},
        "3875": {"comment":"0: the end"},
        "3877": {"comment":"A control code?"},
        "3881": {"comment":"Pushed to $E0 up"},
        "3883": {"synopsis":"$7F and up give '_'.","comment":"$7F up?"},
        "3887": {"synopsis":"'_' for a character that cannot be shown.","comment":"'_'"},
        "3889": {"synopsis":"Stored, DE back by one.","comment":"Stored backwards"},
        "3891": {"synopsis":"The next character.","comment":"Next"},
        "3894": {"synopsis":"Puts B characters of the name at DE as 16-bit units at HL (a long-name entry's part):\nthe $FF end of the name as $0000, every unit after it $FFFF. C carries the state between\ncalls: 1 in the name, 0 past its end.\nExit: DE and HL past what was used; C as above.","comment":"Still in the name?"},
        "3896": {"comment":"No: $FFFF"},
        "3898": {"comment":"A character"},
        "3900": {"comment":"The $FF end?"},
        "3903": {"comment":"$0000"},
        "3909": {"synopsis":"A character: A back to it.","comment":"The character back"},
        "3910": {"synopsis":"A low, C high.","comment":"Low byte"},
        "3912": {"comment":"High byte: C (0, or $FF past the end)"},
        "3914": {"comment":"C to 1 or 0"},
        "3915": {"synopsis":"The next unit.","comment":"Next"},
        "3918": {"synopsis":"Makes the 11-byte short name (8 + 3, padded with spaces, $FF after it) at DE for the\n$FF-ended long name at HL.\n1. Leading spaces and dots are skipped.\n2. Up to 8 characters of the base (SHORT_NAME_CHARS), then the extension: 3 characters\nafter the last dot.\n3. When something was lost (a character changed or dropped, a part too long), '~1' goes\nafter the base at its first space, at most at position 6.\nEntry: HL = the long name, DE = the buffer.\nExit: C = 0 for a faithful name; or C = 1, HL = the '1' of '~1' and B = the room for\ndigits (the state SHORT_TAIL_NEXT takes).","comment":"The buffer kept"},
        "3919": {"comment":"B = 11, C = 0: nothing lost"},
        "3923": {"synopsis":"A leading space or dot skipped.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "3925": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "3929": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "3933": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "3937": {"comment":"The base: 8"},
        "3939": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "3942": {"comment":"The name ended"},
        "3944": {"comment":"Base padded"},
        "3947": {"comment":"The extension: 3"},
        "3949": {"comment":"Its dot found"},
        "3951": {"comment":"Base too long: a dot after it?"},
        "3954": {"comment":"None: no extension"},
        "3956": {"synopsis":"One more dot looked for: HL after the last.","comment":"Another dot?"},
        "3962": {"comment":"Yes: keep looking"},
        "3965": {"synopsis":"HL = after the last dot.","comment":"After the last dot"},
        "3966": {"synopsis":"The extension's characters.","comment":"The extension copied"},
        "3969": {"comment":"All of it?"},
        "3971": {"comment":"No: lost"},
        "3973": {"synopsis":"The rest of the extension padded.","comment":"Padded"},
        "3976": {"synopsis":"$FF after the 11 bytes; '~1' if anything was lost.","comment":"Then $FF"},
        "3979": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "3980": {"comment":"A space in the first 7?"},
        "3982": {"synopsis":"One byte of the base."},
        "3990": {"comment":"None: B = 1"},
        "3991": {"synopsis":"HL = where the '~' would go.","comment":"HL = the space, or position 6"},
        "3992": {"comment":"Anything lost?"},
        "3993": {"comment":"No: C = 0"},
        "3996": {"synopsis":"'~1' at HL; C = 1 digit, HL at the digit.","comment":"'~'"},
        "3999": {"comment":"'1'"},
        "4001": {"comment":"One digit"},
        "4003": {"synopsis":"The name ended in the base: the 3 extension bytes padded too.","comment":"B + 3: the extension too"},
        "4006": {"synopsis":"B spaces, then the end.","comment":"All spaces"},
        "4011": {"synopsis":"The next short name when the last one exists already: the number after '~' goes up by 1;\nwhen it gets a digit more and there is no room to its right, the '~' moves one to the left.\nA name without a tail gets '~1' (carry clear: the exact name exists).\nEntry: HL = the last digit, C = the digits, B = the room for digits (SHORT_NAME_MAKE).\nExit: carry set and HL, B, C updated; or carry clear (A = $1B, rc_dirfull, at 6 digits).","comment":"A tail yet?"},
        "4015": {"comment":"Kept"},
        "4017": {"synopsis":"One digit up, from the last.","comment":"The digit + 1"},
        "4019": {"comment":"Past '9'?"},
        "4023": {"comment":"'0', carry to the left"},
        "4026": {"comment":"More digits?"},
        "4029": {"comment":"All carried"},
        "4031": {"comment":"Room for one more digit?"},
        "4035": {"synopsis":"A digit more: '1' and A zeros after the '~'.","comment":"One digit more"},
        "4037": {"comment":"'1' then zeros"},
        "4039": {"synopsis":"One '0'."},
        "4045": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4047": {"synopsis":"No room: the '~' moves left, unless there are 6 digits.","comment":"Six digits?"},
        "4050": {"comment":"rc_dirfull"},
        "4053": {"comment":"More room"},
        "4055": {"comment":"'~' one to the left"},
        "4060": {"synopsis":"The number went up: carry set.","comment":"Restored"},
        "4064": {"synopsis":"A space: left out, the name marked as changed (C = 1)."},
        "4066": {"synopsis":"Copies up to B characters from the long name at HL to DE for a short name: lower-case\nletters made upper case; a code below $20 or from $80, or + , ; = [ ] becomes '_'; spaces\nand dots that are not the last dot are left out; C = 1 when anything changed.\nExit: Z set at the name's $FF end; carry set at the last dot (HL after it); otherwise\n(B characters taken and more follow) NZ, carry clear, C = 1, HL at the next one.","comment":"Next character"},
        "4068": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "4071": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "4075": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "4079": {"comment":"A control code?"},
        "4081": {"comment":"$80 up?"},
        "4085": {"comment":"'+'?"},
        "4089": {"comment":"','?"},
        "4093": {"comment":"';'?"},
        "4097": {"comment":"'='?"},
        "4101": {"comment":"'['?"},
        "4105": {"comment":"']'?"},
        "4109": {"comment":"Lower case?"},
        "4117": {"comment":"Made upper case"},
        "4121": {"synopsis":"A character not allowed: '_', C = 1.","comment":"'_'"},
        "4123": {"comment":"Changed"},
        "4125": {"synopsis":"The character stored; the next.","comment":"Stored"},
        "4127": {"comment":"Next"},
        "4129": {"comment":"One past the B"},
        "4131": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "4134": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "4138": {"comment":"The last one?"},
        "4143": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "4144": {"synopsis":"More than B characters: NZ, carry clear, C = 1.","comment":"Back to it"},
        "4145": {"comment":"NZ, carry clear"},
        "4147": {"comment":"Too long: changed"},
        "4150": {"synopsis":"A dot: the extension's when no other follows; otherwise dropped.","comment":"A later dot?"},
        "4155": {"comment":"No: the extension's"},
        "4156": {"comment":"Dropped: changed"},
        "4160": {"synopsis":"Looks from HL for a dot before the $FF end.\nExit: carry clear and HL after the dot; or carry set, A = $FE, HL after the $FF.","comment":"Next byte"},
        "4162": {"comment":"The end?"},
        "4166": {"comment":"A dot?"},
        "4171": {"synopsis":"No dot: carry set.","comment":"None: A = $FE"},
        "4174": {"synopsis":"Copies the name of the directory entry at record IY to DE: the long name gathered by\nDIR_ENTRY_FIND (bit 7 of IY+$0D) from ($2F26) up to and with its $FF at $302C; otherwise\nthe short name with a dot (SHORT_NAME_DOT).\nExit: DE after the $FF.","comment":"The destination"},
        "4175": {"comment":"A long name?"},
        "4181": {"comment":"Its start"},
        "4185": {"comment":"Up to $302C, its $FF"},
        "4193": {"comment":"HL = the start"},
        "4194": {"comment":"DE back"},
        "4198": {"synopsis":"No long name: the entry's short name.","comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "4202": {"synopsis":"The 11-byte short name at HL as text at DE: the base without its trailing spaces, '.', the\nextension without them (the '.' left out when there is none), then $FF. Also from $1C62.\nExit: carry set, DE after the $FF.","comment":"The base"},
        "4207": {"comment":"A dot"},
        "4211": {"comment":"The extension"},
        "4216": {"comment":"The last byte"},
        "4218": {"comment":"The dot?"},
        "4222": {"comment":"No: keep it"},
        "4223": {"synopsis":"The $FF end.","comment":"Then $FF"},
        "4227": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4229": {"synopsis":"Copies B bytes from HL to DE with bit 7 cleared, then moves DE back over the trailing\nspaces.","comment":"Trailing spaces 0"},
        "4231": {"synopsis":"One byte.","comment":"The byte, bit 7 off"},
        "4235": {"comment":"Copied"},
        "4237": {"comment":"One more space"},
        "4238": {"comment":"A space?"},
        "4242": {"comment":"No: none trailing"},
        "4244": {"synopsis":"The next byte.","comment":"Next"},
        "4246": {"comment":"Any trailing?"},
        "4249": {"comment":"DE back over them"},
        "4255": {"synopsis":"Stores B spaces at DE (none for B = 0).","comment":"A space"},
        "4257": {"comment":"B = 0?"},
        "4258": {"synopsis":"One space."},
        "4260": {"comment":"Stored"},
        "4264": {"synopsis":"IY = the working directory record at $2E50, IX = its volume's descriptor (its first word).\nA directory record is 15 bytes: +0 the descriptor; +2 bit 7 the FAT16 root area; +3 the\ndirectory's first cluster (4 bytes); +7 the sector in the cluster; +8 the cluster (or the\nroot area's sector); +$0C the entry in the sector, 0-15; +$0D and +$0E the long-name state.","comment":"The working record"},
        "4268": {"comment":"Its descriptor"},
        "4273": {"synopsis":"Sets the directory record IY to the start of the root directory of the volume IX: the\ndescriptor stored, then FAT16's root area (bit 7 of IY+2, cluster 0) or FAT32's root\ncluster (IX+$1D), then DIR_REC_REWIND.\nExit: carry set. BC, DE kept.","comment":"The descriptor"},
        "4283": {"comment":"FAT16?"},
        "4289": {"comment":"FAT32: a cluster chain"},
        "4295": {"comment":"BCDE = the root cluster"},
        "4299": {"comment":"The first cluster"},
        "4307": {"synopsis":"FAT16: the fixed root area, first cluster 0.","comment":"The root area"},
        "4311": {"comment":"Cluster 0"},
        "4318": {"synopsis":"Moves the directory record IY back to its first entry: the current cluster (IY+8) = the\nfirst (IY+3), sector and entry 0.\nExit: carry set. BC, DE kept."},
        "4320": {"comment":"BCDE = the first cluster"},
        "4322": {"comment":"As the current one"},
        "4328": {"comment":"Sector 0"},
        "4332": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "4335": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4337": {"synopsis":"Moves the directory record IY into the directory whose entry it is at: its cluster (the\nhigh word from +$14 on FAT32) as the first; cluster 0 (a '..' to the root) gives\nDIR_REC_ROOT. Then DIR_REC_REWIND.\nExit: carry set; or carry clear and A = the error, $45 (rc_notdir) for a free entry or a\nfile.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4340": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4341": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "4343": {"comment":"A directory?"},
        "4347": {"comment":"Its cluster's low word"},
        "4354": {"comment":"High word 0"},
