        "4386": {"synopsis":"Not a directory: A = $45, carry clear."},
        "4390": {"synopsis":"Moves the directory record IY to its next entry: the next of 16 in the sector; then the\nnext sector, of FAT16's root area (up to IX+$1B) or of the cluster chain ($0577 with the\nfields at IY+7).\nExit: carry set; or carry clear at the end, A = $17 (the root area) or $19 (the chain's\nend), or another error.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "4393": {"comment":"16 done?"},
        "4397": {"comment":"No: success"},
        "4399": {"comment":"The root area?"},
        "4405": {"synopsis":"The next sector of the chain (fields at IY+7 and IY+8); entry 0.","comment":"Next sector or cluster"},
        "4408": {"comment":"End or error"},
        "4412": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "4417": {"synopsis":"FAT16's root area: the next of its IX+$1B sectors.","comment":"BC = the sector index"},
        "4419": {"comment":"+1"},
        "4420": {"comment":"The root area's sectors - 1"},
        "4428": {"comment":"Beyond?"},
        "4430": {"comment":"$17"},
        "4432": {"comment":"Carry clear if beyond"},
        "4434": {"comment":"The new index"},
        "4440": {"comment":"Entry 0"},
        "4445": {"synopsis":"Reads the sector of the directory record IY's entry into the cache: FAT16's root area sector\nIX+$1D + IY+8, or sector IY+7 of cluster IY+8 ($06EE).\nExit: carry set and HL = the 32-byte entry; or carry clear and A = the error.","comment":"The root area?"},
        "4451": {"comment":"BCDE = the cluster"},
        "4453": {"comment":"The sector in it"},
        "4456": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "4459": {"synopsis":"HL = the buffer: the entry's address in it.","comment":"Read error"},
        "4460": {"comment":"The entry number"},
        "4465": {"comment":"x 32"},
        "4471": {"comment":"Plus the buffer"},
        "4474": {"synopsis":"FAT16's root area: its sector IY+8.","comment":"The root area's sector"},
        "4480": {"comment":"+ the index"},
        "4486": {"comment":"The carry to the high word"},
        "4493": {"comment":"Read it"},
        "4498": {"synopsis":"Reads the directory record IY's entry (DIR_ENTRY_ADDR).\nExit: carry set and HL = the entry; Z set for a free entry (first byte 0 or $E5, A = it);\notherwise B = its first byte, A = its attributes, C = byte $0D (a long-name entry's\nchecksum). Carry clear and A = the error when it cannot be read.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4501": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4502": {"comment":"The first byte"},
        "4503": {"comment":"0: never used"},
        "4506": {"comment":"$E5: deleted"},
        "4511": {"comment":"B = the first byte"},
        "4516": {"comment":"A = the attributes"},
        "4519": {"comment":"C = byte $0D"},
        "4521": {"comment":"Success"},
        "4523": {"synopsis":"Finds E free entries in a row in the directory of record IY, from its start: the record is\nleft at the first of them. At the end of the chain a new cluster is linked on ($063E),\ncleared ($0688) and written ($08D1); FAT16's root area cannot grow.\nEntry: E = the entries wanted.\nExit: carry set and HL = the first entry (DIR_ENTRY_READ); or carry clear and A = the\nerror.","comment":"From the start"},
        "4526": {"comment":"None in a row yet"},
        "4529": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4533": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4534": {"comment":"Used?"},
        "4536": {"comment":"The first of a row?"},
        "4541": {"comment":"Its position kept at $201A"},
        "4547": {"synopsis":"One more free entry in the row: enough?","comment":"One more"},
        "4549": {"comment":"Enough?"},
        "4554": {"synopsis":"A used entry: the row starts again.","comment":"Used: none in a row"},
        "4556": {"synopsis":"The next entry; at the chain's end a new cluster.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "4560": {"comment":"There is one"},
        "4562": {"comment":"The root area: full"},
        "4568": {"comment":"BCDE = the last cluster"},
        "4570": {"comment":"A new one linked on"},
        "4573": {"comment":"Cleared"},
        "4576": {"comment":"The cache out"},
        "4579": {"comment":"Moved into it"},
        "4584": {"synopsis":"The directory cannot grow: carry clear."},
        "4586": {"synopsis":"Enough: the record back at the row's first entry.","comment":"Back to the first of the row"},
        "4592": {"comment":"Its entry"},
        "4594": {"synopsis":"HL = IY+7, DE = $201A, BC = 6: the arguments for an LDIR that keeps (or with HL and DE\nswapped restores) a directory record's position (bytes 7-12).","comment":"HL = IY+7"},
        "4601": {"comment":"The copy at $201A"},
        "4604": {"comment":"6 bytes"},
        "4608": {"synopsis":"Looks through the root directory of volume IX, in the working record $2E50, for the volume\nlabel: an entry with attribute bit 3 set, bit 4 clear, that is not a long-name part.\nExit: carry set; Z set and HL = the entry when found, NZ when not (A = 1); or carry clear\nand A = the error.","comment":"The working record"},
        "4612": {"comment":"At the root"},
        "4616": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4619": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4620": {"comment":"Free?"},
        "4622": {"comment":"Attributes"},
        "4625": {"comment":"A long-name part?"},
        "4629": {"comment":"A label, not a directory?"},
        "4634": {"comment":"Found: carry and Z"},
