        "4639": {"comment":"There is one"},
        "4641": {"comment":"None: NZ"},
        "4643": {"comment":"Carry set"},
        "4645": {"synopsis":"Finds the first used short-name entry from the directory record IY's position on, gathering\nthe long name before it (DFIND_NEXT does the same from the next entry):\n1. A long-name part with bit 6 of its number (the last part, which comes first) starts the\nname: the count at IY+$0D, the checksum at IY+$0E, the position kept at $2020, $FF at\n$302C, its characters before it (LFN_ENTRY_TAKE; start at ($2F26)).\n2. Each further part must carry the next lower number and the same checksum; anything else\nstarts again.\n3. A volume label is passed over. At a short-name entry, IY+$0D = $FF when all parts came\nand the checksum of its name (LFN_CHECKSUM) matches; otherwise 0.\nExit: carry set, HL = the entry, E = its attributes; or carry clear and A = the error, $17\nat a first byte 0 (the end).","comment":"No long name yet"},
        "4651": {"synopsis":"Start again from the next entry.","comment":"No long name yet"},
        "4655": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "4658": {"comment":"The end or an error"},
        "4659": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"The entry"},
        "4662": {"comment":"Read error"},
        "4663": {"comment":"Used?"},
        "4665": {"comment":"Deleted: skip"},
        "4668": {"comment":"0: the end, rc_nofile"},
        "4671": {"synopsis":"A used entry: a long-name part or a short name.","comment":"E = the attributes"},
        "4672": {"comment":"A long-name part?"},
        "4678": {"comment":"Its number"},
