        "4845": {"synopsis":"BCDE into the '..' entry.","comment":"Low word at '..'+$1A"},
        "4851": {"comment":"High word at '..'+$14"},
        "4860": {"synopsis":"Is the directory of record IY the root of volume IX? FAT16: bit 7 of IY+2; FAT32: its first\ncluster IY+3 the same as the root cluster IX+$1D.\nExit: carry set for the root. BC, DE, HL kept.","comment":"FAT16?"},
        "4869": {"comment":"BCDE = the root cluster"},
        "4875": {"comment":"BCDE = the record's"},
        "4877": {"comment":"Low words the same?"},
        "4881": {"comment":"High words the same?"},
        "4886": {"synopsis":"Z set when they are the same."},
        "4889": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "4891": {"comment":"No: carry clear"},
        "4893": {"synopsis":"FAT16: bit 7 of IY+2.","comment":"The root area?"},
        "4897": {"comment":"Yes: carry"},
        "4899": {"comment":"No: carry clear"},
        "4901": {"synopsis":"Is the first cluster of the entry at HL BCDE (low word at +$1A, high at +$14)?\nExit: Z set when it is.","comment":"The low word"},
        "4907": {"comment":"Low byte?"},
        "4910": {"comment":"High byte?"},
        "4912": {"comment":"The high word"},
        "4918": {"comment":"Byte 3?"},
        "4921": {"comment":"Byte 2?"},
        "4923": {"synopsis":"Selects file handle A: IY = $2740 + 45 x A, IX = its volume's descriptor (its first word).\nA handle starts with the 15-byte directory record of its entry; +$0F the mode (bit 0 read,\nbit 1 write, bit 6 the position below valid, bit 7 the entry to update); +$10 the sector\nin the cluster; +$11 the cluster; +$15 the byte in the sector; +$17 the file pointer;\n+$1B the first cluster; +$1F the size (4 bytes each).\nExit: B = 0. DE kept.","comment":"B = the handle"},
        "4924": {"synopsis":"HANDLE_SELECT for handle B (from $1760).","comment":"Kept"},
        "4925": {"comment":"One before handle 0"},
        "4932": {"comment":"B + 1 steps"},
        "4933": {"synopsis":"45 bytes per handle."},
        "4937": {"comment":"IX = the descriptor"},
        "4949": {"synopsis":"Is the file at directory record IY in use? (From $171D.)\n1. An open handle (+$0F not 0) whose first 15 bytes are the same record: NZ, carry clear,\nHL = the handle.\n2. Otherwise the file's first sector as the card address ($06C3, $1EC8): when one of the 17\nentries at $2EB4 has it, with the unit + $80 in its first byte: A = 3, carry clear.\nExit: carry set when not in use; or carry clear (as above, or A = a read error).","comment":"16 handles"},
        "4951": {"comment":"From handle 0"},
        "4954": {"synopsis":"One handle."},
        "4956": {"comment":"DE = the record"},
        "4960": {"comment":"15 bytes"},
        "4962": {"synopsis":"One byte of the record.","comment":"The same?"},
        "4970": {"comment":"Open?"},
        "4974": {"comment":"Yes: HL = the handle"},
        "4977": {"synopsis":"The next handle."},
        "4979": {"comment":"Next handle"},
        "4985": {"comment":"The entry"},
        "4989": {"comment":"DE = the cluster's high word"},
        "4996": {"comment":"BC = its low word"},
        "5003": {"comment":"Sector 0 of it"},
        "5007": {"comment":"As the card's address"},
        "5010": {"comment":"BC = its high word"},
        "5012": {"comment":"17 entries"},
        "5017": {"synopsis":"One six-byte entry at $2EB4."},
        "5021": {"comment":"In use, and on this unit?"},
        "5030": {"comment":"Its address"},
        "5037": {"comment":"High words the same?"},
        "5043": {"comment":"Low words the same?"},
        "5051": {"comment":"Found"},
        "5055": {"comment":"A = 3"},
        "5058": {"synopsis":"The next entry.","comment":"Next entry"},
        "5069": {"comment":"Not in use"},
        "5071": {"synopsis":"Is the file pointer of handle IY (+$17) below its size (+$1F)?\nExit: carry set when it is.","comment":"BCDE = the pointer"},
        "5075": {"comment":"BCDE = the size"},
        "5077": {"comment":"Pointer - size"},
        "5082": {"comment":"The high words"},
        "5085": {"synopsis":"Before a byte is written at handle IY's pointer: at or past the end, the size becomes the\npointer + 1.","comment":"Inside the file?"},
        "5089": {"comment":"DE:HL = the pointer"},
        "5092": {"comment":"+ 1"},
        "5102": {"synopsis":"The size of handle IY = DE:HL.","comment":"BC = the low word"},
