        "5647": {"comment":"Carry clear"},
        "5648": {"comment":"DE = the bytes not read"},
        "5653": {"synopsis":"Vector $0145 (ROM 2's WRITE_BLOCK): writes DE bytes from HL to file A at its position.\n1. IY = handle A (HANDLE_SELECT); with C bit 7 = 0, 16K bank C is paged at $C000 (MMU 6 and\n   7) for the source.\n2. Error $1D (rc_number) unless the file is open for writing.\n3. Each sector takes as many bytes as fit from the position: copied into the sector buffer,\n   which is marked changed; the size grows with the position (FILE_SIZE_GROW).\nExit: Fc=1 all written; Fc=0 A = error, DE = bytes not written.\nChanges: $2009 (source pointer), $200B (bytes left).","comment":"IY = handle A's record, IX its volume"},
        "5656": {"comment":"Source pointer"},
        "5659": {"comment":"Bytes left to write"},
        "5663": {"comment":"Keep C, the bank byte"},
        "5664": {"comment":"C bit 7 clear: bank C paged in at $C000"},
        "5669": {"comment":"Open for writing?"},
        "5675": {"synopsis":"One sector's part of the data.","comment":"HL = the position's byte in the sector buffer, DE its offset"},
        "5678": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5680": {"comment":"Keep the buffer address"},
        "5681": {"comment":"HL = room left in the sector ($200 - offset)"},
        "5687": {"comment":"DE = destination in the buffer"},
        "5688": {"comment":"BC = bytes left to write"},
        "5692": {"comment":"Do they all fit?"},
        "5696": {"comment":"No: BC = the room"},
        "5699": {"synopsis":"BC bytes into the sector buffer.","comment":"Keep the chunk's length"},
        "5700": {"comment":"Copy the chunk from the source"},
        "5705": {"comment":"Source pointer moved on"},
        "5708": {"comment":"Sector buffer changed"},
        "5711": {"comment":"BC = chunk length"},
        "5712": {"comment":"Bytes left reduced by it"},
        "5721": {"comment":"Keep Z: nothing left?"},
        "5722": {"comment":"Position + chunk - 1"},
        "5726": {"comment":"Size = position + 1 when passed"},
        "5729": {"comment":"Position + 1"},
        "5733": {"comment":"All written: out through BLK_DONE"},
        "5735": {"comment":"Next sector"},
        "5737": {"synopsis":"Vector $014E (ROM 2's DOS_GET_POSITION): the position of file A.\nExit: DEHL = the position, Fc=1.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5740": {"synopsis":"DEHL = the position (field $17) of the handle at IY; Fc=1.","comment":"BC, DE = position (low, high)"},
        "5742": {"comment":"HL = low word"},
        "5744": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5746": {"synopsis":"Vector $0151 (ROM 2's DOS_SET_POSITION): sets file A's position to DEHL, unchecked.\nExit: Fc=1.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5749": {"synopsis":"Sets the position (field $17) of the handle at IY to DEHL and clears bit 6 of +$0F, so that\nits cluster and sector are found again (FILE_POS_SECTOR).\nExit: Fc=1.","comment":"BC = low word"},
        "5751": {"comment":"Field $17 = the position"},
        "5755": {"comment":"Cluster and sector to be found again"},
        "5761": {"synopsis":"Vector $0154 (ROM 2's DOS_GET_EOF): file A's directory entry details.\nExit: Fc=1 with DEHL = the size, IX = the entry's time and BC its date (MS-DOS form); Fc=0\nwhen the entry cannot be read.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5764": {"comment":"HL = the file's directory entry"},
        "5767": {"comment":"Unreadable?"},
        "5768": {"comment":"Entry + $16: time, then date"},
        "5772": {"comment":"DE = time"},
        "5776": {"comment":"BC = date"},
        "5780": {"comment":"IX = time"},
        "5783": {"comment":"Keep the date"},
        "5784": {"comment":"DEHL = the size"},
        "5788": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5790": {"synopsis":"DEHL = the size (field $1F) of the handle at IY.","comment":"BC, DE = size (low, high)"},
        "5792": {"comment":"HL = low word"},
        "5795": {"synopsis":"Vector $013F (ROM 2's DOS_REF_HEAD): file A's +3DOS header.\nExit: Fc=1, HL = the handle's 8 header bytes (+$23), IX = the header buffer given at open\n(+$2B), NZ when the file has a +3DOS header.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5798": {"comment":"BC = header buffer address"},
        "5800": {"comment":"IX = it"},
        "5803": {"comment":"HL = the handle's header bytes"},
        "5806": {"comment":"File has a +3DOS header?"},
        "5810": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5812": {"synopsis":"Vector $015A: closes file A: its state written (FILE_SYNC), then the handle freed (+$0F =\n0).","comment":"Write the file's state"},
        "5815": {"synopsis":"Frees the handle at IY: its mode byte +$0F = 0.","comment":"Handle free"},
        "5820": {"synopsis":"Vector $0160: writes file A's state to the disk if it is open for writing:\n1. A +3DOS header written again (HEADER_WRITE) when the file has one.\n2. The buffers flushed ($08D1).\n3. The directory entry gets the archive bit, the first cluster, the time and date now and\n   the size, and its sector is written ($0853).\nExit: Fc=1 (also with nothing to do); Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5823": {"synopsis":"FILE_SYNC for the handle at IY (also from $0E9F).","comment":"Nothing to do: Fc=1"},
        "5824": {"comment":"Open for writing?"},
        "5829": {"comment":"Has a +3DOS header? Rewrite it"},
        "5837": {"comment":"Flush the buffers"},
