        "5845": {"comment":"Entry + $0B: attributes"},
        "5849": {"comment":"Archive bit"},
        "5851": {"comment":"Entry + $14"},
        "5855": {"comment":"BC, DE = first cluster (low, high)"},
        "5857": {"comment":"High word at + $14"},
        "5861": {"comment":"Keep the low word"},
        "5862": {"comment":"Time and date now at + $16"},
        "5866": {"comment":"Low word at + $1A"},
        "5870": {"comment":"Keep the size's place"},
        "5871": {"comment":"DEHL = the size"},
        "5875": {"comment":"Size at + $1C"},
        "5882": {"comment":"Write the entry's sector"},
        "5885": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5887": {"synopsis":"Vector $015D: flushes the buffers ($08D1) and frees handle A without updating its directory\nentry.\nExit: Fc=1.","comment":"Keep the handle number"},
        "5888": {"comment":"Flush the buffers"},
        "5892": {"comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5895": {"comment":"Success; free the handle"},
        "5898": {"synopsis":"Vector $0157: changes file A's access mode to C: the file's state is written (FILE_SYNC_IY),\nthen mode C is checked and set as at open (ACCESS_CHECK).\nExit: Fc=1; Fc=0 A = error, the old mode kept.","comment":"IY = handle A's record"},
        "5901": {"comment":"B = the current mode byte"},
        "5905": {"comment":"Write the file's state"},
        "5909": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "5910": {"comment":"Mode 0 while the others are searched"},
        "5914": {"synopsis":"Checks access mode C for the file at IY against its other users and sets it. Mode bits: 0\nread, 1 write, 2 shared (1-3 exclusive, 5-7 shared: DOS_OPEN's access modes), 3 sharing not\nchecked; $10 and up refused.\n1. With +$0F = 0, the other handles and the list at $2EB4 are searched for the same file\n   (FILE_OPEN_CHECK).\n2. In use: allowed with bit 3; refused for an exclusive mode, for shared writing, or when\n   the other user writes without sharing.\n3. Write access to a read-only file: error $1C (rc_ro).\nEntry: B = the mode byte whose high nibble is kept.\nExit: Fc=1, +$0F = B's high nibble + C; Fc=0 A = $1E (rc_denied) or $1C.","comment":"Keep B and the mode"},
        "5915": {"comment":"16 handles"},
        "5917": {"comment":"Same file in use? (Fc=0, A = its mode)"},
        "5921": {"comment":"Mode byte back for now"},
        "5924": {"comment":"Not in use: check the mode"},
        "5926": {"comment":"Bit 3: sharing not checked"},
        "5930": {"comment":"Exclusive mode wanted: refused"},
        "5934": {"comment":"Shared writing wanted: refused"},
        "5938": {"comment":"Other user writes without sharing?"},
        "5944": {"synopsis":"The mode itself: a code below $10; write access only to a file that is not read-only.","comment":"A = the wanted mode"},
        "5945": {"comment":"$10 or more?"},
        "5949": {"comment":"Write access wanted?"},
        "5953": {"comment":"A = the entry's attributes"},
        "5958": {"comment":"Unreadable?"},
        "5959": {"comment":"Read-only file?"},
        "5961": {"comment":"rc_ro"},
        "5965": {"synopsis":"Mode byte = B's high nibble + C; Fc=1.","comment":"Keep the high nibble"},
        "5969": {"comment":"Set the mode"},
        "5972": {"comment":"Success"},
        "5974": {"synopsis":"Refused by the sharing test: A = $24 (rc_inuse) is replaced at once by $1E (ACCESS_DENIED).","comment":"rc_inuse, overwritten by the next load"},
        "5976": {"synopsis":"Error $1E (rc_denied): mode refused.","comment":"rc_denied"},
        "5978": {"synopsis":"Error exit with A kept: Fc=0.","comment":"Fc=0"},
        "5980": {"synopsis":"Vector $0136: opens as handle B the file found by the search record $2E50, or creates it.\nEntry: B = handle (0-15); C = access mode (ACCESS_CHECK); D bit 1 = 1 open the entry found,\n0 create one named by HL ($FF-ended, ENTRY_CREATE); D bit 0 = 0 for a +3DOS header (read\nfrom an existing file, written new in a created one); IX = an 8-byte buffer for the header's\nBASIC bytes, or 0.\n1. The handle filled from the search record and the entry (HANDLE_INIT).\n2. The access mode checked and set.\n3. The header dealt with.\nExit: Fc=1 open; Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"Header buffer address"},
        "5984": {"comment":"IY = handle B's record"},
        "5987": {"comment":"Keep the flags, the mode, the record"},
        "5991": {"comment":"IY = search record $2E50, IX its volume"},
        "5994": {"comment":"Open the entry already found?"},
        "5998": {"comment":"DE = the handle's record"},
        "5999": {"comment":"Fill it from the entry"},
        "6002": {"synopsis":"The access mode, once the handle is filled.","comment":"C = the mode"},
        "6003": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6005": {"comment":"No high bits to keep"},
        "6007": {"comment":"Check and set the mode"},
        "6010": {"synopsis":"Last step: D back, and a header read (D bit 0 = 0).","comment":"D = the flags"},
        "6011": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6012": {"comment":"Header wanted? Read it from the file"},
        "6018": {"synopsis":"New file: its directory entries made first (ENTRY_CREATE).","comment":"Make the entries"},
        "6021": {"comment":"DE = the handle's record"},
        "6022": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6024": {"comment":"Fill it from the new entry"},
        "6027": {"comment":"C = the mode"},
        "6030": {"comment":"Check and set the mode"},
        "6035": {"comment":"D = the flags"},
        "6036": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6037": {"comment":"Header wanted? Write a blank one"},
        "6043": {"synopsis":"Fills the handle record at DE from the search record at IY ($2E50) and its current entry:\n1. The 15 bytes of the directory position copied, the other 30 zeroed; IY = the handle.\n2. +$1B = the first cluster (low word from entry + $1A; high word from + $14 when IX+$13 bit\n   7 is 0, else 0); +$1F = the size (entry + $1C).\n3. +$11, the current cluster = the first.\n4. +$2B = the header buffer address ($2018).\n5. The header bytes copied to that buffer (HEADER_TO_USER).\nExit: Fc=1; Fc=0 when the entry cannot be read.","comment":"HL = search record"},
        "6046": {"comment":"IY = the handle's record"},
        "6049": {"comment":"Directory position: 15 bytes"},
        "6054": {"comment":"Zero the next 30 bytes"},
        "6064": {"comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "6067": {"comment":"Unreadable?"},
        "6068": {"comment":"Entry + $1A: first cluster, low word"},
        "6074": {"comment":"DE = handle + $1B"},
        "6084": {"comment":"Low word of the first cluster"},
        "6089": {"comment":"Skip the high word"},
        "6091": {"comment":"Size from entry + $1C"},
        "6096": {"comment":"16-bit cluster numbers only?"},
        "6100": {"comment":"Then high word 0"},
        "6105": {"comment":"HL = entry + $14"},
        "6109": {"comment":"DE = high word of the first cluster"},
        "6112": {"synopsis":"High word of the first cluster stored.","comment":"+$1D = the high word"},
        "6118": {"comment":"BCDE = first cluster"},
        "6120": {"comment":"Current cluster (+$11) = it"},
        "6124": {"comment":"+$2B = header buffer address"},
        "6133": {"synopsis":"Copies the handle's 8 header bytes (+$23) to the header buffer given at open (+$2B), unless\nthat address is 0.\nExit: Fc=1.","comment":"HL = the handle's header bytes"},
        "6136": {"comment":"DE = the header buffer"},
        "6138": {"comment":"None given? Done"},
        "6142": {"comment":"8 bytes to it"},
        "6147": {"comment":"Success"},
        "6149": {"synopsis":"Makes the directory entries for a new file named by HL ($FF-ended) in the search record's\ndirectory (IY = $2E50):\n1. '.' and '..' refused: error $14 (rc_badname).\n2. The 8.3 form at $202E (SHORT_NAME_MAKE); while an entry already has those 11 bytes, its\n   numeric tail is raised (SHORT_TAIL_NEXT).\n3. One long-name entry per 13 characters, 20 at most (else error $14), and that many plus\n   one free entries in a row (DIR_FREE_FIND).\n4. The long-name entries, from the name's last part: the ordinal (bit 6 on the first\n   written), 13 characters in 16 bits each, attribute $0F, the 8.3 name's checksum; then the\n   8.3 entry: the archive attribute, zeros, the time and date now.\nExit: Fc=1, the search record on the 8.3 entry; Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"Keep the name"},
        "6150": {"comment":"A = first character"},
        "6152": {"comment":"'.'?"},
        "6156": {"comment":"'..'?"},
        "6161": {"comment":"Past the second dot"},
        "6163": {"synopsis":"After the dots: the name's end?","comment":"Name '.' or '..'?"},
        "6165": {"comment":"rc_badname"},
        "6167": {"comment":"Yes: refused"},
        "6170": {"synopsis":"The 8.3 form of the name.","comment":"HL = the name"},
        "6172": {"comment":"8.3 form at $202E"},
        "6178": {"synopsis":"One search of the directory for the 8.3 form at $202E.","comment":"Keep the registers over the search"},
        "6182": {"comment":"From the first entry"},
        "6185": {"synopsis":"One entry.","comment":"A = its attributes"},
        "6188": {"comment":"Free entry?"},
        "6190": {"comment":"Volume label?"},
        "6194": {"comment":"11 bytes"},
        "6199": {"synopsis":"One byte of the two names.","comment":"Same byte?"},
        "6207": {"comment":"Same name: Fc=1"},
        "6210": {"synopsis":"Next entry.","comment":"Next entry: any?"},
        "6215": {"synopsis":"Search over; Fc=1 when the name is taken.","comment":"Registers back"},
        "6219": {"comment":"Name free: the long-name entries"},
        "6221": {"comment":"Raise the numeric tail"},
        "6224": {"comment":"Search again"},
        "6226": {"comment":"No tail left: Fc=0"},
        "6228": {"synopsis":"The 8.3 name is free: the long-name entries counted.","comment":"D = the 8.3 name's checksum"},
        "6235": {"comment":"HL = the long name"},
        "6236": {"comment":"E = entries: one long, one 8.3"},
        "6238": {"synopsis":"13 characters to a long-name entry.","comment":"Up to 13 characters"},
        "6241": {"comment":"Look for the $FF"},
        "6245": {"comment":"Found: counted"},
        "6247": {"comment":"One more entry"},
        "6248": {"comment":"Name ends just after them?"},
        "6251": {"comment":"Then that entry not needed"},
        "6252": {"synopsis":"E entries in all.","comment":"Too many?"},
        "6255": {"comment":"rc_badname"},
        "6258": {"comment":"HL = end of the last 13-character part"},
        "6259": {"comment":"Keep it, the checksum, the count"},
        "6261": {"comment":"Find E free entries in a row"},
        "6264": {"comment":"B = checksum, C = count"},
        "6266": {"comment":"None?"},
        "6267": {"comment":"C = long-name entries"},
        "6268": {"comment":"Bit 6: the last part"},
        "6270": {"synopsis":"One long-name entry, the name's parts from the last.","comment":"Back 13 characters"},
        "6276": {"comment":"Keep the ordinal and the part"},
        "6278": {"comment":"HL = the free entry"},
        "6281": {"comment":"DE = the part"},
        "6283": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6285": {"comment":"Ordinal"},
        "6287": {"comment":"Only the first gets bit 6"},
        "6289": {"comment":"Keep the checksum"},
        "6290": {"comment":"5 characters, padding state 1"},
        "6293": {"comment":"Characters 1-5"},
        "6296": {"comment":"Attribute $0F: a long-name entry"},
        "6299": {"comment":"Type 0"},
        "6302": {"comment":"A = checksum"},
        "6306": {"comment":"Characters 6-11"},
        "6311": {"comment":"Cluster 0"},
        "6316": {"comment":"Characters 12-13"},
        "6321": {"comment":"Sector changed"},
        "6324": {"comment":"Next entry"},
        "6329": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6330": {"comment":"More long-name entries?"},
        "6333": {"comment":"HL = the 8.3 entry"},
        "6337": {"comment":"DE = it"},
        "6338": {"comment":"The 11-byte name"},
        "6348": {"comment":"Attribute $20: archive"},
        "6352": {"comment":"0, spread over bytes $0C-$1F"},
        "6358": {"comment":"HL = entry + $16"},
        "6362": {"comment":"Time and date now"},
        "6365": {"comment":"Sector changed; buffers flushed"},
        "6368": {"synopsis":"Writes the time and date now at HL, 4 bytes in MS-DOS form (from $00F2: DE = time, BC =\ndate).\nExit: HL past them."},
        "6369": {"comment":"DE = time, BC = date"},
        "6373": {"comment":"Time"},
        "6377": {"comment":"Date"},
        "6382": {"synopsis":"Writes a new +3DOS header at the start of the file at IY:\n1. The size made 128 at least; position 0 and its sector fetched (SEEK_START_BYTE).\n2. The 128 bytes: the signature PLUS3DOS_SIG; the file's size; its 8 BASIC header bytes,\n   first taken into +$23 from the header buffer if there is one; zeros; the checksum\n   (SUM_127).\n3. The sector written; position 128, past the header; bit 7 of +$0F set.\nExit: Fc=1; Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"Position 127"},
        "6391": {"comment":"Size 128 at least"},
        "6394": {"comment":"Position 0, HL = its byte in the buffer"},
        "6397": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6398": {"comment":"File has a header"},
        "6402": {"comment":"Keep the header's start"},
        "6404": {"comment":"Signature, 11 bytes"},
        "6412": {"comment":"Keep the place after it"},
        "6413": {"comment":"HL = the handle's header bytes"},
        "6416": {"comment":"BC = header buffer"},
        "6418": {"comment":"DE = the handle's bytes"},
        "6419": {"comment":"HL = the buffer"},
        "6421": {"comment":"None given?"},
        "6425": {"comment":"Its 8 bytes taken"},
        "6430": {"synopsis":"The rest of the header.","comment":"DE = header + 11"},
        "6431": {"comment":"HL = handle + $1F: size, then the 8 bytes"},
        "6438": {"comment":"12 bytes to header + 11"},
        "6443": {"comment":"Zero the next 104 bytes"},
        "6453": {"comment":"HL = the header's start"},
        "6454": {"comment":"Sum of bytes 0-126"},
        "6457": {"comment":"Byte 127: the checksum"},
        "6458": {"comment":"Write the sector"},
        "6461": {"comment":"Position 128: past the header"},
        "6470": {"synopsis":"Reads the +3DOS header of the file at IY:\n1. A file of 128 bytes or more has its first 128 checked (HEADER_CHECK).\n2. Valid: bit 7 of +$0F set; the size and the 8 BASIC header bytes taken from it into +$1F\n   and +$23, copied to the header buffer (HEADER_TO_USER); position 128.\n3. Otherwise HEADER_NONE makes one up.\nExit: Fc=1.","comment":"No header known yet"},
        "6474": {"comment":"DEHL = the size"},
        "6477": {"comment":"Below 128 bytes?"},
        "6483": {"comment":"Then no header"},
        "6485": {"comment":"Position 0, HL = its byte in the buffer"},
        "6488": {"comment":"Failed?"},
        "6490": {"comment":"Signature and checksum right?"},
        "6495": {"comment":"File has a header"},
        "6499": {"comment":"HL = handle + $1F"},
        "6506": {"comment":"12 bytes: size, BASIC bytes"},
        "6509": {"comment":"From header + 11"},
        "6512": {"comment":"Copy to the header buffer"},
        "6515": {"comment":"Position 128: past the header"},
        "6524": {"synopsis":"No header: one made up for a CODE file: type 3, length = the size ($FFFF from 64K up), start\n$4000; copied to the header buffer.","comment":"DEHL = the size"},
        "6527": {"comment":"HL = high word"},
        "6528": {"comment":"64K or more?"},
        "6532": {"comment":"Then length $FFFF"},
        "6535": {"synopsis":"The 8 bytes at +$23.","comment":"HL = the handle's header bytes"},
        "6538": {"comment":"3 zeros at the end"},
        "6541": {"comment":"Type 3: CODE"},
        "6543": {"comment":"Length"},
        "6547": {"comment":"Start $4000"},
        "6551": {"synopsis":"One of the last 3 bytes zeroed."},
        "6555": {"comment":"Copy to the header buffer"},
        "6558": {"synopsis":"Checks the 128 bytes at HL for a +3DOS header: byte 127 the sum of bytes 0-126, bytes 0-10\nPLUS3DOS_SIG.\nExit: Z valid, DE = HL + 11; NZ not."},
        "6559": {"comment":"A = sum of 127 bytes"},
        "6562": {"comment":"Checksum right?"},
        "6563": {"comment":"DE = the header"},
        "6565": {"comment":"The signature"},
        "6568": {"comment":"11 bytes"},
        "6570": {"synopsis":"One signature byte.","comment":"Same?"},
        "6578": {"synopsis":"HL = IY + $23, the handle's 8 header bytes."},
        "6586": {"synopsis":"Fc=1 when the search record's entry is not a dot entry (name starting '.'); Fc=0 A = $1E\n(rc_denied) when it is, or when the entry cannot be read.","comment":"HL = the entry"},
        "6590": {"comment":"Name starts with '.'?"},
        "6593": {"comment":"rc_denied"},
        "6598": {"synopsis":"Position 0 for the file at IY, its sector fetched: HL = that byte in the sector buffer\n(FILE_BYTE_ADDR).\nExit: Fc=1; Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"DEHL = 0"},
        "6606": {"comment":"HL = the byte in the buffer"},
        "6609": {"synopsis":"A = the sum of the 127 bytes at HL; HL moves past them."},
        "6610": {"comment":"127 bytes"},
        "6612": {"synopsis":"One byte added."},
        "6617": {"synopsis":"The 11 bytes that start a +3DOS header: \"PLUS3DOS\", $1A, $01, $00. HEADER_WRITE writes them;\nHEADER_CHECK compares them."},
        "6628": {"synopsis":"Reads entries from the search record's position until one passes:\n1. One entry into the buffer at DE (vector $0139, DIR_ENTRY_GET).\n2. The attribute filter C (DIR_FILTER).\n3. With B bit 5, the name must match the pattern at HL (NAME_MATCH).\n4. Rejected: with B bit 1, CAPS SHIFT + SPACE stops the search; then the next entry (vector\n   $013C with A = 0).\nEntry: HL = pattern ($FF-ended), DE = buffer, B = options (bit 6 passed on to\nDIR_ENTRY_GET), C = filter.\nExit: Fc=1 an entry found, in the buffer; Fc=0 at the end, an error or BREAK.","comment":"Keep pattern, buffer, options"},
        "6631": {"comment":"Vector $0139: next entry to the buffer"},
        "6639": {"comment":"IX = buffer"},
        "6642": {"comment":"End or error?"},
        "6643": {"comment":"Does the filter pass it?"},
        "6646": {"comment":"Yes: the name"},
        "6648": {"synopsis":"Rejected: BREAK allowed?","comment":"Break test wanted?"},
        "6652": {"comment":"Keyboard row with SPACE"},
        "6656": {"comment":"SPACE pressed?"},
        "6659": {"comment":"Row with CAPS SHIFT"},
        "6663": {"comment":"CAPS SHIFT too?"},
        "6664": {"comment":"BREAK: Fc=0"},
        "6665": {"synopsis":"Next entry.","comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "6669": {"comment":"Vector $013C, A = 0: one entry on"},
        "6677": {"comment":"DE = buffer"},
        "6680": {"comment":"Try it"},
        "6682": {"synopsis":"Filter passed: the name, if a pattern is wanted.","comment":"Pattern wanted?"},
        "6684": {"comment":"No: found"},
        "6686": {"comment":"Keep the registers"},
        "6691": {"comment":"BC = buffer"},
        "6692": {"comment":"DE = pattern"},
        "6693": {"comment":"BC = 8.3 name at buffer + 1"},
        "6694": {"comment":"HL = name text at buffer + 30"},
        "6700": {"comment":"Does the name match?"},
        "6706": {"comment":"Yes: found"},
        "6708": {"comment":"No: on"},
        "6710": {"synopsis":"DIR_FIND_NEXT's filter on the entry at IX (attributes, then the 8.3 name); C's bits reject:\n7 files, 6 directories, 5 directories whose name starts '.', 4 hidden or system entries.\nExit: Z passes, NZ rejected.","comment":"A = attributes"},
        "6713": {"comment":"Directory?"},
        "6717": {"comment":"Directories rejected?"},
        "6720": {"comment":"Dot directories rejected?"},
        "6724": {"comment":"Name starts with '.'?"},
        "6729": {"comment":"A = attributes again"},
        "6734": {"comment":"A dot directory: NZ"},
        "6737": {"synopsis":"A file: files rejected?","comment":"Files rejected?"},
        "6740": {"synopsis":"Hidden and system entries.","comment":"Rejected?"},
        "6743": {"comment":"Hidden or system: NZ"},
        "6746": {"synopsis":"Unpacks a record of DIR_ENTRY_GET at HL: its name text (length at + $1C) copied to DE,\n$FF-ended; then DE = time, BC = date, IX = the size's low word, HL its high word.","comment":"Keep the record"},
        "6747": {"comment":"Record + $1C: name length"},
        "6755": {"comment":"Name text to DE"},
