        "7592": {"synopsis":"Vector $0181 (ROM 2's PATH_CALL, DE = $FF00): drive A's current path. B = 0 changes it to\nthe path at HL; B = 1 writes it to the buffer at HL, $FF-ended; other B go to $3D01 in\nDivMMC RAM. These are IDE_PATH's rc_path_change (0) and rc_path_get (1). The work ($1DB3)\nruns through $040D in the RAM bank that the drive's table byte ($0204) names.\nExit: Fc=1; Fc=0 A = error.","comment":"Keep the drive in IYH"},
        "7594": {"comment":"A = the drive's table byte"},
        "7597": {"comment":"Call $1DB3 in that RAM bank"},
        "7603": {"synopsis":"PATH_OP's work: B = 0 change, 1 get, others at $3D01.","comment":"B = 0?"},
        "7607": {"comment":"Not 1: in DivMMC RAM"},
        "7611": {"comment":"Keep the buffer"},
