        "7669": {"synopsis":"Fetches drive A's path record (254 bytes from DivMMC RAM bank 9 at $2000 + 256 x drive) to\nDE + 2 and makes it text: 'X:' and the path, or 'X:/' when the record is not valid (byte 0\nthe complement of byte 1, whose low nibble is the drive) or the path does not start with a\nseparator. With bit 6 of the drive's table byte, byte 1's high nibble goes before the letter\nin decimal. A byte outside $21-$7F ends the text.\nExit: HL = the text, DE on its $FF, C = byte 1 (the drive byte).","comment":"Two bytes free before the record"},
        "7671": {"comment":"Drive number"},
        "7674": {"comment":"HL = $2000 + 256 x drive"},
